            <ArticleTitle>Capsaicin patch (Qutenza) for postherpetic neuralgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The FDA has approved a topical 8% patch formulation of capsaicin (Qutenza-NeurogesX), available only by prescription, for local treatment of postherpetic neuralgia. Postherpetic neuralgia occurs after herpes zoster in about one third of patients ≥60 years old and can persist for months or even years.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
